# ==============================================================================
# GITIGNORE PROPERTIES - REPOSITORY HYGIENE CONTROL
# ==============================================================================
# PRINCIPLE: Keep the repository pristine. Never track machine-specific configurations,
# local virtual environments, or compiled system cache files in a public repository.
#
# Why this matters:
# 1. Environment Pollution: Virtual environments (.venv) contain thousands of dependency 
#    files specific to your laptop's operating system. Tracking them breaks the repository 
#    for other developers and floods your Git history with useless noise.
# 2. Local Workflow Isolation: VS Code settings and workspace configurations are personal 
#    preferences. They do not belong in a shared, public code exhibit.
# 3. Cache Management: Python auto-generates '__pycache__' folders to speed up execution. 
#    These are transient binary files that clutter version control and should never be pushed.
# ==============================================================================

# Ignore Python virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Ignore local editor settings and workspaces
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Ignore Python execution cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ignore local mock database files generated during tests
*.db
